%description:

The interference floor an external cell imposes, against the closed form.

An ExtCell is not a node: it is a transmit power, a position and a band
allocation policy, which the UE's channel model turns into interference in
computeExtCellInterference. The fingerprint suite barely sees it: in the
lte/multicell Interference-* family, switching it off moves only the
statistics hash. This grades the floor it adds.

Worth having separately from BackgroundCellFloor, which covers a background
cell, because the external-cell path is not the same code: it reads the
cell's band status rather than a background scheduler's allocation, and it
has no load of its own to vary. With FULL_ALLOC the cell occupies every band
in every TTI, so the interference is a constant and the SINR one number --
there are no idle TTIs to reach, unlike InterferenceDelta and
BackgroundCellFloor:

    S = txPower   - PL_38901(d_serving) + Gtx + Grx - cableLoss
    I = extPower  - PL_36814(d_extCell) + Gtx + Grx - cableLoss
    N = thermalNoise + noiseFigure

The interferer's path loss is computeExtCellPathLoss's: always the TR 36.814
formulas, whatever propagation study the model itself is configured with,
and the straight distance between the two positions, heights included, as
both the 3D and the 2D one. enableExtCellLos is switched off, so the link is
NLOS by configuration rather than by borrowing the serving link's LOS state.

Both of the walk's branches are asserted: the CQI computation reads the
cell's band status of the current TTI (measuredSinrDl), a data reception the
previous TTI's (rcvdSinrDl). With extCellInterference off each statistic is
the quiet budget; on, each is the loaded budget, and in both cases a single
value.

%extraargs: -c ExtCellFloor

%file: demo.xml
<config>
    <interface among='eNB* eNodeB* enb* *Enb* gNB* gNodeB* gnb* *Gnb* upf* *Upf* mecHost* pgw*' address='10.x.x.x' netmask='255.255.255.0'/>
    <interface hosts='*' address='192.168.x.x' netmask='255.255.255.0'/>
</config>

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[Config ExtCellFloor]
output-scalar-file = results/${iterationvarsf}${repetition}.sca
output-vector-file = results/${iterationvarsf}${repetition}.vec
network = simu5g.simulations.lte.networks.MultiCell
sim-time-limit = 3s
**.routingRecorder.enabled = false
cmdenv-express-mode = true
cmdenv-status-frequency = 10000000s
seed-set = 0
**.vector-recording = false
**.measuredSinrDl.result-recording-modes = mean,count,min,max
**.rcvdSinrDl.result-recording-modes = mean,count,min,max

############### The sweep: the one thing that varies ##############
**.extCellInterference = ${eci = false, true}
**.downlinkInterference = false
**.uplinkInterference = false
**.bgCellInterference = false

############### Geometry: the victim 100 m from its cell, 500 m from the external cell ##############
# The other cell and its UEs are far away and idle; downlink interference is
# off in any case.
*.eNodeB1.mobility.initialX = 300m
*.eNodeB1.mobility.initialY = 300m
*.eNodeB1.mobility.initialZ = 25m
*.eNodeB2.mobility.initialX = 1900m
*.eNodeB2.mobility.initialY = 1900m
*.eNodeB2.mobility.initialZ = 25m
**.ue1*.servingNodeId = 1
**.ue2*.servingNodeId = 2
*.ue11.mobility.initialX = 400m
*.ue11.mobility.initialY = 300m
*.ue11.mobility.initialZ = 1.5m
*.ue12.mobility.initialX = 300m
*.ue12.mobility.initialY = 400m
*.ue12.mobility.initialZ = 1.5m
*.ue2*.mobility.initialX = 1900m
*.ue2*.mobility.initialY = 1800m
*.ue2*.mobility.initialZ = 1.5m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMinX = 0m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMinY = 0m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMinZ = 0m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMaxX = 2000m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMaxY = 2000m
**.mobility.constraintAreaMaxZ = 50m
**.mobility.initFromDisplayString = false

############### The channel: one path loss and nothing else ##############
**.cellularNic.channelModelType = "Tr38901ChannelModel"
**.scenario = "URBAN_MICROCELL"
**.nodebHeight = 25m
**.ueHeight = 1.5m
**.dynamicLos = false
**.fixedLos = true
**.fading = false
**.shadowing = false
**.enableExtCellLos = false

############### The budget terms, stated rather than inherited ##############
*.carrierAggregation.numComponentCarriers = 1
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0].carrierFrequency = 2GHz
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0].numBands = 6
**.numBands = 6
**.eNodeBTxPower = 40dBm
**.antennGainEnB = 18dBi
**.antennaGainUe = 0dBi
**.cableLoss = 2dB
**.thermalNoise = -104.5dBm
**.ueNoiseFigure = 7dBm

############### One external cell, occupying every band ##############
*.numExtCells = 1
*.extCell[0].positionX = 900m
*.extCell[0].positionY = 300m
*.extCell[0].positionZ = 25m
*.extCell[0].txPower = 40dBm
*.extCell[0].txDirection = "OMNI"
*.extCell[0].carrierFrequency = 2GHz
*.extCell[0].numBands = 6
*.extCell[0].bandAllocationType = "FULL_ALLOC"

############### Traffic: a trickle to the victim ##############
*.ue*.numApps = 1
*.server.numApps = 1
*.ue*.app[0].typename = "CbrReceiver"
*.ue*.app[0].localPort = 3000
*.server.app[0].typename = "CbrSender"
*.server.app[0].destAddress = "ue11"
*.server.app[0].destPort = 3000
*.server.app[0].localPort = 3088
*.server.app[0].packetSize = 40B
*.server.app[0].samplingTime = 0.02s
*.server.app[0].startTime = 0.1s

*.configurator.config = xmldoc("./demo.xml")

%postrun-command: ../../physics_reference.py --grade results >verdict.txt

%contains: verdict.txt
graded=11 failures=0

%not-contains: verdict.txt
FAILED
